## Why This Is Asked
This probes governance at scale: per-tenant safety, data residency, and cost-aware routing in a live Azure OpenAI pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-aware policy packs in blob storage
- PDP (policy decision point) in Azure Functions
- Data residency routing to OpenAI regional endpoints
- Redaction and guardrails before outbound calls
- Auditing and observability via Azure Monitor

## Code Example
```javascript
function evaluatePDP(tenantId, metadata, policies) {
  const policy = policies[tenantId] || policies["default"];
  // residency check
  if (policy.residency && policy.residency !== metadata.region) return { action: "block" };
  // budget constraint
  if (typeof policy.budget === "number" && metadata.cost > policy.budget) return { action: "redirect", destination: "onPrem" };
  // allowed destination
  if (policy.allowedDestinations?.includes("OpenAI")) return { action: "allow", destination: "OpenAI" };
  return { action: "block" };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test PDP edge cases (missing tenant, malformed metadata, policy drift)?
- How would you implement zero-downtime policy updates and per-tenant rollbacks?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a privacy-preserving, multi-tenant AI workflow at scale, with strict data isolation, governance, and measurable latency.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant OpenAI deployment and prompt routing
- Real-time ingestion (Event Hubs) and low-latency scoring
- KB grounding via Cognitive Search on Blob data
- PII redaction (Text Analytics) and per-tenant masking (Key Vault)
- RBAC (Azure AD), Data Lake auditing, canary rollout

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: route prompt for tenant, redact, ground, respond
async function handleRequest(req){
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  const raw = req.body;
  const redacted = redactPII(raw);
  const kb = loadKBVersion(tenantId);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(redacted, kb, tenantId);
  const resp = await openai.complete(prompt, {deployment: getDeployment(tenantId)});
  logAudit(tenantId, prompt, resp);
  return resp;
}
```

